---
import Growth from '../../layouts/Growth.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/growth/Hero.astro';
import AdviceCta from '../../components/growth/AdviceCta.astro';
import { afterAgency, postSchema } from '../../data/advice-wave-b';
const post = afterAgency;
---

<Growth
  title={post.title}
  description={post.description}
  schema={postSchema(post)}
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <Hero eyebrow={post.eyebrow} title={post.h1} intro={post.lede} />
  <article class="section wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <a class="back-link" href="/advice">
        ← Advice
      </a>
      <h2>Separate hurt feelings from missing results</h2>
      <p>
        Screenshots of reach, clicks, or “leads” are not booked jobs. A report
        can be accurate and still leave the calendar quiet.
      </p>
      <p>
        Write down what you paid, what you were promised, and what showed up on
        the calendar. That list is your brief for the next conversation. Bring
        it. Do not rebuild it from how the meetings felt.
      </p>
      <h2>Questions that expose a pitch deck</h2>
      <p>
        Ask these on the call. A pitch deck gets soft here. An operator answers.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          What counts as a result—<strong>appointments that show</strong>, or
          form fills?
        </li>
        <li>Who answers the phone / follows up, and in what time?</li>
        <li>
          What do you need from us weekly so the guarantee (if any) is fair?
        </li>
        <li>
          Can I see examples in my trade or a close one, with calendar outcomes?
        </li>
        <li>What happens to the assets if we stop—pages, ads accounts, CRM?</li>
        <li>What will you not promise?</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Question 4 is about jobs on a calendar, in your trade or a close one.
        One public home-service example is{' '}
        <a href="/work/gonzalez-and-sons-roofing">Gonzalez &amp; Sons Roofing</a
        >: around two roofs a month, then around eight. That is their result,
        not a number for your business.
      </p>
      <h2>Red flags that usually repeat</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Blame only “your closers” with no intake review. If nobody looked at
          missed calls, the closers are not the whole story.
        </li>
        <li>
          Refusal to define a lead. If a click, a form, and a shown appointment
          all count the same, you do not have a result.
        </li>
        <li>
          Long contracts before a clear 90-day scoreboard. Know what working
          means before the term locks.
        </li>
        <li>
          Channel worship (more Facebook, more SEO) with no booking math.
          Traffic that never becomes an appointment is a bill.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <AdviceCta />
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What “good” looks like in the first 30 days</h2>
      <p>In the first month you should see the work, not a new slogan.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A shared scoreboard: spend, conversations, bookings, and show rate.
        </li>
        <li>One owner on their side who replies in business hours.</li>
        <li>
          Changes based on missed calls and no-shows—not only creative tests.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If the month is only new ads and new graphics, they have not looked at
        the phone.
      </p>
      <h2>How to walk into the next call without getting sold</h2>
      <p>
        Bring the last 90 days of calendar and ad spend. Rough is fine. The gap
        between what you paid and what got booked is the brief.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ask them to diagnose before they pitch a package name. The phone, the
        follow-up, and the calendar come first.
      </p>
      <p>
        If they lead with plan ladders and prices before they understand intake,
        leave.
      </p>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        {post.faq.map((item) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{item.q}</summary>
            <p>{item.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p>
        <a href="/advice">Advice</a>·
        <a href="/advice/lead-response-time">
          How fast you answer is the real cost of a lead
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
  <AdviceCta headline={post.ctaHeadline} body={post.ctaBody} />
</Growth>
